system@niuhep.physics.niu.edu wrote:
> 	I am telnetting to the unix machine from a decterm that is logged 
> into a vms machine.  The DECterm is set at 48 lines and I would like
> to be able to use all 48 lines, rather than having to change the size
> of the DECterm to 24 lines to accomodate the telnet screen.

Use `stty rows 48` to use all 48 lines.  See `man stty` for more 
information.

> 	Second, I would like to be able to search multiple directories
> for a file.  I have been able to do the following:

Use `ls -R' to get a listing for the current directory and all
directories below it.  'ls -lR' for a long listing.  See the man
page for ls for more information.

If you just want to find a specific file use:

	find . -name file_name -print

To find the file "file_name" in any directory below the current one.

Hope this helps

Ian



