> Got an info from Digital Local here in Jakarta that the fast Ethernet card
> DE500-XA is not
> work properly yet on Alpha 2100  under OSF/1 .... is any body using this
> card ? .. any problem ?

We've had DE500-XAs in a pair of 2100s for over a year now, with no 
noticeable problems.  Those machines are running 3.2c and whatever version
of the firmware came with 3.2c (I believe the firmware disc was V3.3).

We've recently tried sticking another DE500-XA in each of our 2100s, though,
and met with less success (the additional cards failed to show up in the 
console 'show dev' or 'show config' output on either machine).  According to 
the person I spoke with from DEC support, DEC *now* says that 3.2d & the 
accompanying firmware is the minimum rev to support the DE500-XA, though 
we've been running 3.2c and the DE500-XA in 100Mb (half-duplex) mode for 
over a year.

The release notes for the 2100 firmware on the V3.6 firmware disc claims
that version of the firmware fixes problems with the DE500-XA support,
including full-duplex support.  After upgrading one of our 2100s to the
latest firmware revision and 3.2g, both DE500-XAs show up at the console
>>> prompt and appear to be working just fine.

In short, if you're running the latest firmware and 3.2d or later on
your 2100s, I think you'll have good success with the DE500-XA.

Tim
