Pui Ming WONG wrote:
> 
> We run Digital Unix 3.0 with 256Mb memory. Owing to more users
> putting up their httpd on the system, the default immediate mode
> of swap space allocation always have swap down to 10% free
> Hence i changed it to deferred mode and this problem is solved.
> However, it appears that the system is much slower than it used
> to be. Don't know if it has anything to do with the deferred mode
> swap space allocation or it's just a wrong feeling.

Running in deferred mode will allow you to allocate more virtual
memory, which may in turn lead to an increase in the demand for physical
memory.  Thus the system may now be paging / swapping when it wasn't
before (in eager swap mode).  Use the vmstat command to see if this
is the case.

Pat

