Curt Smith wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> We'd like to upgrade our DUX cluster to v4.0a + newest ASE. But
> we have customers with DUX 3.2d in the field and don't want to 
> orphan them or force ourselves to buy more DEC boxes.
> 
> Is there any experiences with backward compatibility of 
> executables linked on DUX 4.0 running or NOT running on 3.2d-2?
 
Since DUX 4.0 was a major functional release there are many new
symbols in the V4.0 libraries that do not exist in the V3.2x libraries.
This is especially true of libc.  

Although backward compatibility isn't guaranteed, we have run some
V4.0 images on V4.2x with success.  If you're going to try it, 
at least make sure your V4.0 images are linked non_shared to improve
the chances of it working.  
 
Joe



