Yes, there is a NetWorker client for Digital UNIX.  There are
a few methods of getting it.  If you install the SingleServer
off the base OS cd, you get the client part included (plus
lots of other space hogging executables).  You can order the
Digital Client Kit (includes UNIX and NT alpha clients).  And
if you get the Layered Product CD, or whatever they call it
now, then you could load the client subset off of that (latest
version will be 4.2A on the next LPCD due out soon).  Regardless
of the method of getting the client software, the server system
must be configured with client licenses.

You can search the Software Product Descriptions (see Digital's
home page, pick search, limit search to Software Product Descriptions,
choose NetWorker as the search word) to see what is available.

Digital information is listed in the Legato web pages, although the
information there isn't always kept as up to date as possible.

