If you're just doing machine-to-machine copy, there are lots of solutions:

	=> tar cf - /path/blah | (rsh decbox 'cd /destination; tar sxvf -')
	=> as above but use "cpio"
	=> as above but use "dd"
	=> NFS-mount the SCO partitions to the DEC UNIX machine and do a "tar"
	   or "cp -r" from the network disk to the local one
	=> NFS-mount the DEC UNIX partitions to the SCO machine and do a "tar" 
	   from the network disk to the local one

If you have to involve the tape drive, the NFS solutions could be used to
create the tape dump, and then just dump back from tape.  As long as the
same O/S is being used to create the backup, you should be fine.
