Marc Elsen wrote:
> 
> I will be installing a Alphastation 255 in what
>  could be called a "Mission Critical Environment".
> 
>  How do I disable the "Star Energy" mode of the monitor
>  (model = VCR21-W3) ?
> 

In DU 4.0, the energy star behavior of the monitor can be controlled
using the application:

/usr/bin/X11/dxpower

It allows you to turn off the standby, suspend, and off modes for the
monitor, as well as the 'slow down CPU' and 'spin down disks' energy
saving features of the AlphaStation 255.

Alternatively, if you don't want to use a lovely GUI, you can use the
'xset(1X)' command and use the -dpms option.



