but on an AlphaStation 500 ("DEC_KN20AA") it works without a hitch.

2. In order to be able to use the system as a regular workstation the
system is equipped with a graphics adapter which the kernel identifies
as a ZLXp-E with 4 MB map size. Does this mean it's a ZLXp-E1, E2 or
E3 and furthermore - how do we get it do display more than 1024x768
pixels? Do we need the Open3D product to do this?

Any help is appreciated.

Thanks
/Erik



