Erik Persson (erik@stravinsky.ikp.liu.se) wrote:
: We recently recieved an Alphaserver 1000 4/266 with Digital Unix 4.0
: but there are two major problems:

: 1. The kernel can't be rebuilt. ld fails with an unresolved symbol
: "ace_regbase". This occurs as soon as the "DEC1000" cpu type is
: defined in the config file. I don't know which cpu types this affects,
: but on an AlphaStation 500 ("DEC_KN20AA") it works without a hitch.

Boot the generic kernel, and run sizer to make a new configuration
file; "sizer -c -n FOO" will put the new config file in /tmp/FOO,
then (replace FOO with whatever you want, I suggest you save your old
config file until you've built a new kernel):

% mv /tmp/FOO /sys/conf/
% cd /sys/conf
% ./config FOO
% cd /sys/FOO
% make depend && make

Stephen
