	Just set the ethernet parameter in the console to thinwire.

	Don't let it autoselect.  Also, ensure that you do not have an
AUI or 10BT cable connected and that you do have your thinnet
connected and it is properly terminated.  Finally, those TULIPs are
very sensitive to total cable load and will complain about thinnet
arrangements that work for other hosts.  I would suggest a "T"
connector with two terminators until you have it working OK. i.e. a
dead ended net.

	We get the PCI junk as well.  I don't know what it means.

	Good luck,

