I'm not sure why Adobe doesn't have a viewer out for Digital UNIX,
since they already have a UNIX port for other flavors...

The later versions of ghostscript can interpret most .pdf files.  The
only real problem is that the you can't use ghostview to browse
through the .pdf file (there's actually a way to do this, apparently,
but it involves patching an old version of ghostscript --- I tried
this briefly, but gave up after having lots of problems).

The easiest way to use ghostscript like this is to use the included
shell script "pdf2ps" to convert the .pdf file into a standard
PostScript file, and then use ghostview to view the PostScript.  It's
slow, and takes a lot of disk space, so it's not an optimal method,
but at least it works.

