For what it's worth, I recently ported stel to OSF/1 (most of the way
- file transfer's busted, but telnet-like functionality works nicely).

stel does D-H key exchange, followed by 3-DES, DES, IDEA or RC4
encryption.  3-DES is the default.  This means you don't have to
distribute keys, before you start using it.

Key generation is a bit pokey on a sun IPC, but acceptable on a
contemporary machine from any vendor.  The encryption doesn't slow
things much at all.

