: In article <515uu5$o3e@newton.cc.rl.ac.uk>,
: I wrote:
: >If a process forks off a child to do some work for it dbx says
: >
: >"New child attached. Use switch to gain access to process nnnnnn"

: Perhaps the main (attached) program is waiting for input at that point?

No - in the case I referred to the main program called a function which ran
up a c-shell to expand some file names. I tried to step over this function
call but I was still caught by dbx.

