I ran into the very same problem with GNU make. It's the POSIX support
that's at fault. I just edited the fnmatch.h header distributed by GNU thus

#if 1 // !defined (_POSIX_C_SOURCE) || _POSIX_C_SOURCE < 2 || defined
(_GNU_SOURCE)
#define	FNM_FILE_NAME	FNM_PATHNAME /* Preferred GNU name.  */
#define	FNM_LEADING_DIR	(1 << 3) /* Ignore `/...' after a match.  */
#define	FNM_CASEFOLD	(1 << 4) /* Compare without regard to case.  */
#endif

Peter Hegelund 

 



