In article <DxMFxJ.KxH@news.cern.ch>, pai@sp053.cern.ch (Alan Paic) writes:
|>Hi!
|>
|>Does anyone know how to use vrestore to look at a different save set 
|>than the first on a given tape? Namely, I am using Exabyte tapes and
|>it seems a pity not to use one tape to back up several disks, but when 
|>I do so (using vdump repeatedly with -N), vrestore seems to want to 
|>look only at the first backup save set. The man page doesn't mention 
|>anything about this. Is it possible that I have to use a different 
|>Exabyte for each disk??? Is there some other software or workaround?
|>		Thanks a lot,
|>					Alan
|>

Check the man page for vrestore. It mentions that the default device is
/dev/rmt0h, which automatically rewinds the tape. To prevent this, specify
a norewind device name with the "-f" option. (eg, vrestore -t -f /dev/nrmt0h
to list the files; you can use "mt fsf [count]" to skip forward [count]
files, "mt bsf" to skip backwards, etc.)

David Potterveld (potterveld@anl.gov)



