Jorge Prates (Jorge.Prates@navier.ist.utl.pt) wrote:
: Why do I get 
: # a.out
: Unable to obtain requested swap space
: Segmentation fault (core dumped)

Maybe your a.out is demanding more virtual than you think?

Also, your DEC box may still be in the default, agressive swap
mode.  If you have the sym-link: /sbin/swapdefault
then try mv'ing it to another name and re-booting.  This changes the
swap behavior to "lazy" mode, and will consume less swap and
leave process and data in RAM until more physical RAM is demanded.

Good luck.

curts@compgen.com




