newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Hi all,

just a word of warning.

DECnsr (Legato Networker) uses what ever tape density is set by what ever
utility that  last accesses the tape drive prior to NSR starting.

This problem is extenuated when NSR also uses the low density tape device
immediately after a power off/on reboot.

What happend to my last backup was the system lost power for a few moments
about half an hour before the unattended backup started.  When it did start it
saved the files in low density format to the tape unit.  Even though the
"Devices" list clearly shows /dev/nrmt0h (h for high density) is been used.  This
meant that the follwoing morning there wasn't enough tapes or time to complete
the backup.

All I have to do to rectify this problem is do a tar or dump or cpio or dd to the
same device and then NSR starts working in high density mode again.  Of
course this work around doesn't work on unattended backups that start at
midnight.

To be fair the system is configured so :

    DEC 3000/500
    Digital UNIX 3.2d
    TLZ06 DAT 2/4GB tape drive

It may be limited to systems with tlz06's ???   Has anybody else seen this
behaviour?

If so, is there a work around ?

Reagrds,

Walter Zambotti



