A program (dwrap.c) which mitigates the problem(s) above 
with using dump from cron is available in the archive:  
 
    ftp://ftp.u.washington.edu/public/noyd/bdump.tar
 
Another characteristic of 'cron' not mentioned above is that it 
will schedule another job regardless of how the previous run of the
job ended (or did not end).  If jobs do not terminate in a timely manner,
cron can be killed or otherwise foiled when it runs out of resources
(account/process limits).
