#
#DECnsr (Legato Networker) uses what ever tape density is set by what ever
#utility that  last accesses the tape drive prior to NSR starting.
[rest of story deleted for brevity]

Well, you are jumping the gun here in assuming what is wrong.
A problem with certain 4mm drives (usually with changers) has been
noted where the device does not reset itself properly and doesn't
have the density set when accessed at certain points.  That is a
firmware problem, from all I've heard, and I don't know if a fix has
been made available or whether the exact problem is known.  Some
things will reset the device, possibly you see that behavior when you
do tar/dump/etc (you don't say whether you are using the rmt#h device
or not though).  Resetting the bus probably will work as well.  NetWorker
(note DECnsr is the ULTRIX product and it isn't called Legato NetWorker
on Digital UNIX) is just a product which exposes the problems.

#If so, is there a work around ?

I suggest you contact your customer support center and open a problem
report.  That way when the firmware which fixes the problem is 
released, you should be in line to get a copy of it.  This supposes
that you already have the system under contract.  I have no idea 
how you would get that firmware if you aren't under contract. 

To keep up with others using the NetWorker family of products, I
suggest you join the NetWorker mailing lists... listed at
http://www.legato.com/mail_list/mail_list.html or note that just
the unix centered list is mentioned on
http://www.iphase.com/NetWorker/ (archives also listed there).

regards,

A. Lenox
