How about uname -av ?  Or if you can't map revision to letters, try 
% strings /vmunix | grep `uname -v` | egrep 'UNIX|OSF'

>The reason I am asking is that upgrading to Dec unix 4.0 the system
>should be at least 3.2G. And I don't which 3.2 we have with our systems.

I don't think that's correct. To upgrade to 4.0 requires at least 3.2C
for an update installation. If you install 3.2G, the 3.2G release
notes state that you will *not* be able to do an update installation to
get to 4.0.  This is because 3.2G supports hardware (like the
AlphaStation 500/400) which 4.0 doesn't.  When the next release after
4.0 arrives, you may be able to do an update installation from 3.2G to
that. 

Hope this helps,

Drew




