Xinfu Xia <xia@femto.med.unc.edu> writes:

> Dear Experts:
> 	Where is exportfs on this OSF1 machine?
> There is a file /etc/exports.  Can I export the directories listed in
> the file
> manully?

There is no exportfs on Digital Unix. What you will have to to i to
restart the NFS services (or at least mountd). You can set up a script
to do this:

Restarting all the NFS-stuff:

--->snip<---
#!/bin/sh
/sbin/init.d/nfs stop
/sbin/init.d/nfs start
--->snip<---

Restarting mountd:

--->snip<---
#!/bin/sh
/sbin/kill -HUP `/sbin/ps -e | /bin/grep mountd | grep -v grep |\
	/bin/awk '{print $1}'`
--->snip<---

/Erik



