> : Not so. (Really, I'm talking from experience.) I do subscribe to your
> : line of reasoning, but Solaris is not the the way to. No platform that
> : has sizeof(int) == sizeof(long) resp. sizeof(int) == sizeof(void*)
> : should be your choice in this case.
> : 


Don't make the mistake of thinking that this is platform dependent.  I've worked
on platforms where one compiler had sizeof(int) == sizeof(long) and a compiler
from another vendor had sizeof(int) < sizeof(long).  The relationship of int and
long is not a platform issue but an implementation detail.  (Of course the
specs say that sizeof(int)<=sizeof(long) ).  I've seen other compilers where
this was dependent on compiler flags.

