DECunix 4.0 in the current release is a workstation version not a
server version. Servers should use versions >3.2D-2 (depend on
used hardware). Version 4.0a/4.1 will fully support servers.

Be sure the adapter is supported on your machine! 
If the adapter will be supported, check the ECU 1.8 disk. The ECU 
setup detects the hardware and loads the parameter file from the ecu
disk to setup the controller correctly for later use. If the requested
parameter file could not be found the hardware is not official supported
by DEC, that's my experience!

You can also try the eisa setup parameter file from a DOS-System, because
the ECU disk is also a FAT Disk.

