In article <01bb96a6$f4a4d000$99f1acce@NONE.sympatico.ca>, "Luc Marotte" <luc.marotte@boulevard.ca> says:
>
>Which of LSM, UFS and ADVFS s the best file system ?
>
>
UFS is the standard Unix filesystem. IT should be used for the root
partition of your system. Disadvantage: Backups should be made in
single user mode, because unix will corrupt open files during 
backup.

Advfs should be used for larger partitons (>= 1GB). Advantages:
no filesystemcheck necessary at boottime (=faster boot) because
it is transaction controlled and you can add single partitions to
a virtual disc (= domains). You need a licence to use advanced tools
like the graphical gui, balancing or to create complex domains.
With advfs you have the capability to create online backups which
is not possible with UFS.

LSM is the logical storage manager to produce mirrored disk and to
use advanced features of the storage works technologie.

Suggestion:
Use UFS for the root partition and for all data partitions (includes
/usr and /var) ADVFS.

Regards

                                



