: Can someone help me with the syntax for a "find" command, that will only
: find executable programs.  I've wandered through the Man pages for find
: many times, and I just cant seem to figure it out.  I want to find it if
: it's executable by anyone (owner, group, world).

This version will find anything with any execute bit set:

% find -perm -0111

This one restricts the search to only things of type file (excluding
directories and symlinks):

% find -type f -perm 0111

