Take a look at http://xoweb.xopen.org/public/tech/aspen/lp64_wp.htm

This document describes the programming model to be used for 64-bit 
computing. The model preferred was LP64 (sizeof(int) < sizeof(long)).

Some of the companies participating (HP, Sun, etc?) are already using the 
LLP64 model (sizeof(int) == sizeof(long) < sizeof(long long)).

So how are HP and Sun going to move to 64-bit computing? Migrating the 
existing programking model and porting existing applications? Supporting 
two models at once (with two versions of system header files and 
difficulties linking libraries compiled with different models)? What?

